{# TM·02 — NEEDS A DECISION, and the pane COLLAPSES TO NOTHING when nobody does.

   A pane that stayed on screen to report that nothing is wrong would spend the
   top of the page saying so, every visit, forever. So the whole plate is
   guarded: no rows, no widget.

   THREE KINDS OF ROW, AND THE THIRD IS NOT LIKE THE OTHER TWO. Rows one and two
   are TASKS — they have a done, so they carry the control that reaches it. Row
   three is a STANDING RISK: an installation with one Super Admin has no
   recovery path if that account is lost, because the model has no break-glass,
   no second owner and no audit trail. It carries no action, because resolving
   it means promoting somebody, and that is a decision rather than a button on a
   warning. It does not go away by being read.

   NOTHING HERE IS DISMISSIBLE. Every row is a live query, so the only way to
   clear one is to change the fact underneath it. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/team/_bits.html.twig' as bits %}

{% if overview.needsAttention %}
<div class="c" data-tm>
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">TM&middot;02</span>Needs a decision<span class="src">&middot; {{ overview.attentionCount }} &middot; nothing here is dismissible</span></span>

    <div class="tm-att">
        {# ACTIVE ACCOUNTS ONLY. Somebody who has never signed in AND has been
           deactivated is deliberately absent: the decision this row asks for has
           already been taken about them, and a pane that kept chasing a
           switched-off account is a pane nobody trusts. #}
        {% for person in overview.neverSignedIn %}
            <div class="tm-attrow w">
                {{ bits.icon_mail() }}
                <div class="at">
                    <b>{{ person.fullName }} has never signed in</b>
                    <p>
                        {%- if person.wasInvited -%}
                            <b>{{ person.invitedBy ? person.invitedBy.fullName : 'Somebody since removed' }} invited them {{ bits.ago(person.invitedAt) }}</b>
                            and the verification token is still unused &mdash; so the invitation was sent, and they
                            have not arrived.
                        {%- else -%}
                            <b>Nobody invited them</b> &mdash; this account was created with a password rather than
                            invited, so there is no link outstanding and nothing to resend. Somebody has to hand
                            the password over, or send a reset link from the person's own record.
                        {%- endif -%}
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="ad">
                    <a class="softbtn" href="{{ path('team_member', {uuid: person.uuidString}) }}">Open {{ person.firstName }}</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}

        {% for person in overview.holdNothing %}
            <div class="tm-attrow w">
                {{ bits.icon_info() }}
                <div class="at">
                    <b>{{ person.fullName }} holds nothing</b>
                    <p>Staff, and with no position &mdash; so <code>PermissionVoter</code> falls through to
                    <code>position?-&gt;hasPermissionValue()</code> and denies every capability there is. They can
                    reach the sign-in screen and then no page behind it.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="ad">
                    <a class="softbtn acc" href="{{ path('team_member', {uuid: person.uuidString}) }}">Give them a position</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}

        {% if overview.soleSuperAdmin %}
            <div class="tm-attrow r standing">
                {{ bits.icon_warn() }}
                <div class="at">
                    {% if overview.isFirstRun %}
                        <b>You are the only account on this installation</b>
                        <p>Nothing here is broken &mdash; this is what a fresh install looks like. It is worth
                        knowing before you go any further that if this one account is lost there is no second
                        owner and no recovery path in the model. <b>A second administrator is the first thing
                        worth adding.</b></p>
                    {% else %}
                        <b>There is one Super Admin: {{ overview.soleSuperAdmin.fullName }}</b>
                        <p>The only account that can switch user, and the only one that survives every permission
                        check by tier. If it is lost there is no second owner, no break-glass and no audit trail
                        to reconstruct from &mdash; the installation is administered from a database client or not
                        at all. It is also why this account cannot be demoted or deactivated: the code refuses,
                        and it unlocks the moment somebody else holds the tier. <b>This does not go away by being
                        read.</b></p>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
                {% if overview.isFirstRun %}
                    <div class="ad"><a class="softbtn acc" href="{{ path('team_invite') }}">Add a person</a></div>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
